{"repositoryId":1171238294,"availability":"available","full":"GradientHQ/symphony-coord","name":"symphony-coord","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1082,"forks":166,"created":"2026-03-03T02:30:53Z","updated":"2026-10-10T05:32:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://symphonycoord.ai/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.431Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.431Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.431Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.431Z","stars":1082,"forks":166}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Task & Plan-K → Capability-Guided Screening (CGS) → Contextual Bandit Routing (CBR) & CoT-P → Aggregate & Learn","Symphony-Coord is a task-local routing framework for multi-agent LLM systems. It formulates subtask-level executor selection as an online contextual bandit problem, using task information and observable service state.","Instead of relying on static expert assignment or handcrafted orchestration policies, Symphony continuously learns routing decisions from interaction outcomes."],"features":["Task & Plan-K: form candidate plans and ordered subtask chains.","Capability-Guided Screening (CGS): retain a Top-L shortlist using capability match, prior success, and reliability.","Contextual Bandit Routing (CBR) & CoT-P: select executors with LinUCB and collect repeated subtask outputs.","Aggregate & Learn: combine outputs by subtask-level majority voting and weighted cross-plan voting, then update the selector when action-linked feedback is resolved.","capability-guided, non-executing Top-L screening"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GradientHQ/symphony-coord/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9b6d12caba4b03dd9f4b9f17f6644fdfd5d78f2dfce8d552f2250667cff01690","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.569Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:16:26.569Z","projectInsights":{"ve